  "phase_3": {
    "user_prompt": "Now I want to establish the baseline water quality from locations most isolated from human influence. Please group the three 'Roof downspout' sites together (sites 440416103151700, 440155103162100, and 440444103132800). Calculate the overall median Total Suspended Solids (TSS) concentration (in micrograms per liter (µg/L)) across all samples collected from these three sites combined during the study period.",
    "expected": 15000.0,
    "unit": "ug/L"
  },
  "phase_4": {
    "user_prompt": "Next, we need to understand how E. coli concentrations change as stormwater moves into receiving structures. \n\nFirst, group the remaining sites as follows:\n- Parking lot: 440416103151900, 440154103162100, 440156103161800, 440445103132900\n- Street curb: 440417103152202, 440150103162300, 440202103161600\n- Channel/storm sewer: 440429103151300, 440430103151000, 440436103151400, 440201103161500, 440445103132700, 440445103132600\n\nWhat is the overall median E. coli concentration across all samples from the 'Channel/storm sewer' sites? \n\nAdditionally, create a bar chart showing the median E. coli concentration for all four infrastructure types (Roof downspout, Parking lot, Street curb, and Channel/storm sewer) to visualize the contamination pattern. Save this plot as `infrastructure_ecoli_medians.png`.",
    "expected": 1800.0,
    "unit": "mpn/100 mL",
    "checkpoint": {
      "enabled": true,
      "reference_conclusion": "E. coli concentrations are lowest in samples collected from locations most isolated from human influence (roof downspouts, median ~4 mpn/100 mL) and highest in the downstream receiving channels and storm sewers where stormwater is aggregated (median ~1,800 mpn/100 mL). Parking lots and street curbs have intermediate levels (medians of ~220 and ~150 mpn/100 mL, respectively).",
      "requires_visual_evaluation": true,
      "expected_visual_filename": "infrastructure_ecoli_medians.png",
      "visual_description": "A bar chart displaying median E. coli concentrations for four categories. The bars should roughly reflect the following values: Roof downspout (~4), Street curb (~150), Parking lot (~220), and Channel/storm sewer (~1800).",
